# Swap the relocalization map on the device at runtime.
#
# This transfers the given file to the device relocalization map path (file
# transfer channel). On firmware that supports it, if the device is currently in
# reloc mode (map_mode == 2) and SLAM is running, finishing the transfer makes
# the device asynchronously restart SLAM and reload the new map (see
# Host_USB_Slam_Mode_Protocol.md). If map_mode != 2 or SLAM is not running, the
# new map simply takes effect at the next SLAM start.
#
# The transfer may take a while, so it runs in a background thread: success/rc
# below only report whether the request was *accepted*. The actual transfer
# result is logged by the driver. Only one map transfer can run at a time.
#
# map_path : absolute path to the relocalization map file (.bin).
string map_path
---
bool success            # true if the transfer request was accepted
int32 rc                # 0=accepted, -1=invalid/missing file, -2=another transfer in progress, -100=device not ready
